course: dictionary
lesson: 13916
title: Lazybones and playful teasing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lazybones is a lazy person, someone who does not want to get up or do any work. You can guess this from the words around it: «Get up, lazybones, the bus is coming!» Getting up and catching a bus are clues that the word is about someone who is slow to start the day.
explain: This word is playful and informal, a joke rather than an insult. When a parent says «You lazybones!» with a smile, they are teasing, not being cruel. Tone matters, so think about how the person sounds and what is happening around them.
explain: Lazybones is the same in the plural, so one lazybones and two lazybones both look the same. Notice that it is a noun, a word for a person. Use it in chatty talk, not in formal writing.
fact: A lazybones is a lazy person, someone who does not want to get up or do any work.
fact: «Lazybones» is informal, so it sounds friendly in chatty speech.
fact: Phrases you may hear are «come on, lazybones» and «you lazybones».
fact: The plural is also lazybones: «The two lazybones slept until noon.»
fact: It is usually a playful tease, not a serious insult, so the tone of voice shows how it is meant.
exercise: «Get up, lazybones, the bus is here!» What is a lazybones? | A kind of breakfast cereal | *A lazy person who does not want to get up | A bus driver
exercise: Mum laughs and says, «You lazybones!» Is she cross or teasing? | Asking for help with the washing up | Very sad and upset | *Teasing in a playful way | Furious and shouting
exercise: Which word is the plural of lazybones? | lazybone | lazybonies | lazybonesses | *lazybones
test: Ella says «Come on, lazybones!» to her brother still in bed. What does she mean? | He is a famous doctor | He has lost his shoes | He is an excellent runner | *He is a lazy person, and she is teasing him
test: Which sentence uses lazybones correctly? | «The lazybones ran a race and won.» | *«The two lazybones slept through the film.» | «I lazybones my homework every night.» | «The lazybones was a very loud bell.»
exam: «Grandad is a lazybones who loves his armchair.» What does lazybones mean here? | A fast runner who wins races | A type of armchair | *A lazy person who avoids work | A very hard worker who never stops
